This project uses a tiered licensing model based on version numbers (vx.y).
Let x denote the latest major version and y denote the latest minor version.

IMPORTANT NOTICE ON HISTORICAL VERSIONS:

  Versions v9 and earlier were developed and released as proprietary
  commercial software by Yunnan Solar Corona Technology Co., Ltd. They are
  NOT open source and are NOT covered by any open-source license, including
  the MIT License. All rights to those versions are reserved. No source code,
  binaries, or other materials from v9 or earlier are licensed under the terms
  of this document.

The open-source licensing model described below applies ONLY to v10 and later.

The applicable license depends on the version:

  Part A — v(x-1) and earlier open-source versions   → MIT License
  Part B — vx, previous minor releases               → Competition-Exclusion License (commercial use allowed)
  Part C — vx latest minor and dev branches           → Non-Commercial & Competition-Exclusion License

When a new minor version is released, the previous minor version transitions
from Part C to Part B. When a new major version is released, the previous
major version transitions from Part B to Part A (MIT License).

  Example timeline:
    v10.0 released → v10.0 is Part C
    v10.1 released → v10.0 becomes Part B, v10.1 is Part C
    v11.0 released → all v10.x become Part A (MIT), v11.0 is Part C

  Note: This MIT transition (Part A) will first take effect when v11 is
  released, making v10.x the first versions to receive the MIT License.
  Versions v9 and earlier remain proprietary and are never relicensed.

